{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 51,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have mercy upon me, O God, according to thy lovingkindness:\nAccording to the multitude of thy tender mercies blot out my transgressions.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wash me thoroughly from mine iniquity,\nAnd cleanse me from my sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I know my transgressions;\nAnd my sin is ever before me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Against thee, thee only, have I sinned,\nAnd done that which is evil in thy sight;\nThat thou mayest be justified when thou speakest,\nAnd be clear when thou judgest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I was brought forth in iniquity;\nAnd in sin did my mother conceive me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou desirest truth in the inward parts;\nAnd in the hidden part thou wilt make me to know wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Purify me with hyssop, and I shall be clean:\nWash me, and I shall be whiter than snow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make me to hear joy and gladness,\nThat the bones which thou hast broken may rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hide thy face from my sins,\nAnd blot out all mine iniquities.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Create in me a clean heart, O God;\nAnd renew a right spirit within me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cast me not away from thy presence;\nAnd take not thy holy Spirit from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation;\nAnd uphold me with a willing spirit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then will I teach transgressors thy ways;\nAnd sinners shall be converted unto thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Deliver me from bloodguiltiness, O God, thou God of my salvation;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my tongue shall sing aloud of thy righteousness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Lord, open thou my lips;\nAnd my mouth shall show forth thy praise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou delightest not in sacrifice; else would I give it:\nThou hast no pleasure in burnt-offering.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit:\nA broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do good in thy good pleasure unto Zion:\nBuild thou the walls of Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.51.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.51.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then wilt thou delight in the sacrifices of righteousness,\nIn burnt-offering and whole burnt-offering:\nThen will they offer bullocks upon thine altar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "A contrite sinner’s prayer for pardon.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician. A Psalm of David; when Nathan the prophet came unto him, after he had gone in to Bath-sheba.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
